        "semantic-avi-v1"
      ],
      "license": "MIT",
      "testOnly": true,
      "homepage": "https://github.com/frabert/riff",
      "rationale": "🫥️ RECLASSIFIED, on the same ground as `gltf`, `png`, `jpg`, `bmp` and `tiff`. The `riff` crate does real work — it parses and composes genuine RIFF chunks — but what a MUTATION SHOULD PRODUCE is computed by this owner's own `🦀️oracle.rs`, 1069 lines whose header states outright that \"every type, parser and writer below is a fresh, independent implementation\", and whose `apply_kind` returns `mutation kind {other} has no oracle implementation` for anything it does not cover.\n\nBoth halves then read the same specification, so a misreading of it yields two agreeing wrong answers. `riff` discharges \"the result is a well-formed AVI\", NOT \"the mutation computed the right answer\" — only the second is what a mutation oracle is for. A required SUPPLEMENT, never a substitute.\n\nThe 22 third-party-generated fixtures registered alongside are unaffected and stay: real AVI bytes composed by `riff`, byte-reproducible, and exactly what a qualifying reader gets pointed at on the day one exists.",
      "hostPath": "✏️s/🔌️plugins/🗄️stdio/🧪️oracle/📦️packages/🦀️rust",
      "kind": "cross-semio-implementation",
